    {
      "text": "dispensation of fulness of times, D&C 27:13 (76:106; 112:30; 121:31; 124:41; 128:18–20; 138:48, 53). observe commandment concerning teaching until fulness of scriptures is given, D&C 42:15. fulness of earth is yours, D&C 59:16. those in celestial glory receive fulness and glory of the Father, D&C 76:20, 56, 94 (88:29). those in terrestrial and telestial glories receive of the Lord’s glory but not fulness, D&C 76:76–77, 86. Lord’s rest is fulness of his glory, D&C 84:24. the Father gave of his fulness to the Son, D&C 93:4, 12, 16, 19, 27. the Son received not fulness at first, D&C 93:12–13. the Son continued from grace to grace until he received fulness, D&C 93:13. if faithful, Saints to receive fulness of John’s record, D&C 93:18. no man receives fulness unless he keeps commandments, D&C 93:27. spirit and element, inseparably connected, receive fulness of joy, D&C 93:33 (138:17). fulness of scriptures to be printed, D&C 104:58. receive fulness of the Holy Ghost, D&C 109:15. fulness of priesthood revealed, D&C 124:28. everlasting covenant instituted for fulness of the Lord’s glory, D&C 132:6.",
